cing the damaged cable to the technician.\",\n      \"correct_under_reading\": false,\n      \"reading_status\": \"contradicts_stem\",\n      \"convention_evidence_ids\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"option\": \"D\",\n      \"strongest_reading\": \"A revised delivery schedule might make delivery early, but the passage says noticing the fault delayed delivery.\",\n      \"correct_under_reading\": false,\n      \"reading_status\": \"contradicts_stem\",\n      \"convention_evidence_ids\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"blocking_defects\": [],\n  \"style_notes\": [\n    \"The short narrative clearly distinguishes Nila’s immediate response from later events.\"\n  ],\n  \"cuet_fit\": {\n    \"criteria\": {\n      \"syllabus_objective\": {\n        \"level\": 3,\n        \"evidence\": \"Recognising the sequence of events is a core reading-comprehension skill for narrative passages.\"\n      },\n      \"format_authenticity\": {\n        \"level\": 2,\n        \"evidence\": \"Workable four-option comprehension MCQ; no matched authenticated comparator was supplied.\"\n      },\n      \"level_calibration\": {\n        \"level\": 2,\n        \"evidence\": \"Straightforward chronology comprehension; no matched authenticated comparator was supplied, so calibration is tentative.\"\n      },\n      \"discrimination_value\": {\n        \"level\": 2,\n        \"evidence\": \"Several distractors reuse later narrative actions, testing whether the candidate tracks event order.\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"reasoning_steps\": 1,\n    \"estimated_difficulty\": \"easy\",\n    \"cognitive_level\": \"comprehension\",\n    \"exemplar_ids_compared\": []\n  },\n  \"option_resolution\": [\n    {\n      \"option\": \"A\",\n      \"status\": \"contradicted\",\n      \"false_part\": \"straight to the community hall\",\n      \"premise_source\": \"passage_scope\",\n      \"evidence_id\": \"E1.1\",\n      \"premise_quote\": \"After replacing the damaged cable, the technician tested the lamp. Nila then carried the working lamp to the community hall.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The passage places repair and testing before Nila carries the lamp; that is not her immediate response.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"option\": \"B\",\n      \"status\": \"contradicted\",\n      \"false_part\": \"herself\",\n      \"premise_source\": \"passage_scope\",\n      \"evidence_id\": \"E1.1\",\n      \"premise_quote\": \"After replacing the damaged cable, the technician tested the lamp.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The passage assigns replacing the cable to the technician, not Nila.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"option\": \"C\",\n      \"status\": \"supported\",\n      \"false_part\": \"\",\n      \"premise_source\": \"excerpt\",\n      \"evidence_id\": \"E1.1\",\n      \"premise_quote\": \"She switched off the power and asked the technician to inspect it.\",\n      \"reason\": \"These are the actions the passage places immediately after Nila notices the flicker.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"option\": \"D\",\n      \"status\": \"contradicted\",\n      \"false_part\": \"the delivery would be early\",\n      \"premise_source\": \"passage_scope\",\n      \"evidence_id\": \"E1.1\",\n      \"premise_quote\": \"She told the organiser that noticing the fault had delayed the delivery but prevented them from using a damaged cable.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The passage says the fault delayed delivery, not that delivery would be early.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
